Blind Touch includes the OpenArm v2 robot model (MJCF and meshes) by Enactic, from
https://github.com/enactic/openarm_mujoco, licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(blindtouch/scenes/assets/LICENSE-openarm).

Changes from the original (blindtouch/scenes/openarm_right.template.xml):
  * only the right arm is kept;
  * position servos are replaced by torque (motor) actuators;
  * joint frictionloss is set to zero (friction is a per-episode realism effect);
  * the hand is generated in two variants: a true gripper holding a free tool by
    friction, and a rigid nominal hand with the tool as a known payload.

The rest of the code is MIT licensed (LICENSE).
